@startuml
' Focus: successful persistence of one evaluated attempt, before combat resolution.
' File operations and saveIfHigher validation/comparison are summarized in notes.
title Preserve the best attempt before rotating history
hide footbox
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
participant "game:GamePlayState" as game
participant "history:SaveStore" as history
participant "best:LeaderboardStore" as best

activate game
game -> history : save(result)
activate history
history -> history : loadHighScore()
activate history
history -> best : load()
activate best
best --> history : Optional<SavedRecord>
deactivate best
opt high-score file is missing
    history -> history : load()
    activate history
    history --> history : latest history records
    deactivate history
    opt history contains at least one record
        history -> best : saveIfHigher(existingBest)
        activate best
        best --> history
        deactivate best
    end
end
history --> history : Optional<SavedRecord>
deactivate history
history -> best : saveIfHigher(candidate)
activate best
note over history, best
  Reload and validate the current best.
  Write only if absent or beaten by WPM, then accuracy.
  Lower scores and exact ties leave the file unchanged.
end note
best --> history
deactivate best
history -> history : read history; append candidate; retain latest ten
activate history
deactivate history
history -> history : writeSafely(...)
activate history
note right of history
  Inherited from FileStore: write a temporary file,
  then replace history and clean up the temporary file.
end note
deactivate history
history --> game : return
deactivate history
note over game, best
  Successful path shown. Initialization precedes history rotation.
  The high-score and history writes are separate, not a transaction.
  An IOException aborts save(); GamePlayState reports it and still calls
  CombatEncounter.submitTypingResult(result). Run autosaving is omitted.
end note
deactivate game
@enduml
